{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Core Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/MachineLearningWorkflow","doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/TimeSeriesForecasting"],"anchor":"Core-Guides"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"A complete guide to columnar data loading, O(1) indexing, zero-allocation row iteration, group-by aggregations, joins, and machine learning exports.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with SwiftSci DataFrame","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftDataFrame"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftdataframe\/gettingstarted"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftDataFrame"},{"type":"text","text":" is an immutable, columnar data analysis engine built natively in Swift 6 for Apple Silicon. It combines Apache Arrow \/ Feather zero-copy memory buffers, O(1) schema lookups, and SIMD bitmask filtering."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["DataFrame (Value Type: Immutable Struct + Copy-On-Write)","┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐","│ Schema (FieldMap: O(1) dictionary lookup by column name)    │","├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤","│ Column 0: TypedColumn<Int64>   [ 101, 102, 103, 104 ]       │","│ Column 1: TypedColumn<String>  [ \"A\", \"B\", \"A\", nil ]       │","│ Column 2: TypedColumn<Double>  [ 12.5, 45.0, 33.2, 98.1 ]   │","└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"1. Loading Datasets (CSV, Feather & Parquet)","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Loading-Datasets-CSV-Feather--Parquet"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Load data from local files or memory buffers using streaming asynchronous APIs:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Foundation","import SwiftDataFrame","","\/\/ 1. Load CSV with automatic delimiter and type inference","let csvURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"passengers.csv\")","let df = try await DataFrame(csv: csvURL)","","print(\"Loaded DataFrame: \\(df.shape.rows) rows x \\(df.shape.columns) columns\")","df.head(5).debugPrint()","","\/\/ 2. Load binary Feather \/ Apache Arrow IPC format (Zero-Copy)","let featherURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"dataset.feather\")","let featherDF = try await DataFrame(feather: featherURL)","","\/\/ 3. Load compressed Apache Parquet format","let parquetURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"telemetry.parquet\")","let parquetDF = try await DataFrame(parquet: parquetURL)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"2. O(1) Column Access & Zero-Allocation Row Iteration","type":"heading","anchor":"2-O1-Column-Access--Zero-Allocation-Row-Iteration"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Access typed columns by name or iterate through rows using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DataFrameRowSequence"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ 1. O(1) Typed Column Subscript","if let ageCol = df[column: \"Age\", as: Double.self] {","    let meanAge = ageCol.mean","    print(\"Mean Age: \\(meanAge ?? 0.0)\")","}","","\/\/ 2. Zero-Allocation Row Iteration (Bypasses heap dictionary creation)","for row in df.rows {","    if let city = row.string(\"City\"), let score = row.double(\"Score\") {","        if score > 90.0 {","            print(\"Top Performer in \\(city): Score = \\(score)\")","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"3. High-Performance Filtering & Feature Transformation","type":"heading","anchor":"3-High-Performance-Filtering--Feature-Transformation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Filter datasets using SIMD bitmasks or transform columns functional-style:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ 1. Fast condition-based filtering","let filtered = try df.filter(column: \"Fare\", where: .greaterThan(50.0))","","\/\/ 2. Predicate filter closure","let adultFirstClass = df.filter { row in","    (row.int(\"Pclass\") == 1) && ((row.double(\"Age\") ?? 0) >= 18.0)","}","","\/\/ 3. Add calculated feature column","let engineeredDF = try df.addColumn(\"FarePerYear\", as: Double.self) { row in","    guard let fare = row.double(\"Fare\"), let age = row.double(\"Age\"), age > 0 else { return nil }","    return fare \/ age","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"4. GroupBy Aggregations & Joins","type":"heading","anchor":"4-GroupBy-Aggregations--Joins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group by categorical columns and aggregate numeric columns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ 1. GroupBy with Mean Aggregation","let deptAverages = df.groupBy(\"Department\").mean()","deptAverages.debugPrint()","","\/\/ 2. High-Performance SIMD Hash Join","let employees = try DataFrame(columns: [","    TypedColumn<Int64>(name: \"id\", values: [1, 2, 3]),","    TypedColumn<String>(name: \"name\", values: [\"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\"])","])","let departments = try DataFrame(columns: [","    TypedColumn<Int64>(name: \"id\", values: [1, 2, 3]),","    TypedColumn<String>(name: \"dept\", values: [\"AI\", \"Cloud\", \"Security\"])","])","","let merged = try employees.join(departments, on: \"id\", how: .inner)","merged.debugPrint()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"5. Exporting Flat 1D Matrices for ML","type":"heading","anchor":"5-Exporting-Flat-1D-Matrices-for-ML"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Export tabular data directly into contiguous flat buffers for machine learning training:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let (flatMatrix, rows, cols) = try df.toFlatFeatureMatrix([\"Age\", \"Fare\", \"Pclass\"])","print(\"Generated flat feature matrix: \\(rows) samples x \\(cols) features.\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/GettingStarted"},"references":{"doc://SwiftDataFrame/documentation/SwiftDataFrame":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"High-Performance Columnar Data Tables built on Apache Arrow.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftdataframe","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame","role":"collection","title":"SwiftDataFrame","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftDataFrame/documentation/SwiftDataFrame/TimeSeriesForecasting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/TimeSeriesForecasting","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftdataframe\/timeseriesforecasting","role":"article","title":"Time Series Decomposition & Forecasting with SwiftForecast","abstract":[{"text":"Perform classical time series decomposition, SARIMA forecasting, and Kalman filtering.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftDataFrame/documentation/SwiftDataFrame/MachineLearningWorkflow":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"End-to-end Machine Learning pipelines using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftML"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftPreprocessing"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCluster"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftdataframe\/machinelearningworkflow","title":"Machine Learning Workflow with SwiftML","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/MachineLearningWorkflow"}}}